# threshold-ledger — the mesh's scattered inline magic numbers as ONE data file
# (uxn-threshold-ledger, gates-as-data stage 2, 2026-07-23). Each row is a calibrated
# predicate: params are the RUNTIME inputs, consts are the CALIBRATED numbers (k=v pairs,
# naturals only), the template is the s-expr the pinned evaluator runs. Recalibration is a
# diff on the consts column of THIS file, never a script edit; consumers resolve their
# defaults through `mesh-sexpr-gate --const <gate> <k>` (env > ledger > inline fallback),
# and mesh-rom-calibrate --ledger drives every row through ./threshold-fixtures against a
# native-shell twin (DIVERGE = expression/evaluator drift; 16-bit overflow = DOMAIN).
#
# evaluator-sha1: b3c917e97894502018735e15d3448aee92b59ffb   (lisp-eval.rom)
#
# format: name | params (runtime inputs, bound positionally) | consts k=v… | template
# clear-fresh:  1 FRESH · 0 STALE — mesh-clear's handoff budget (was MESH_CLEAR_FRESH_SECS 900 inline)
# load-gate:    0 SKIP-quiet · 1 PROCEED · 2 SKIP-load — l1c is centi-load1 (load1*100),
#               thr = nproc*k centi = nproc*0.90 (was DEFAULT_THR awk n*0.9); quiet [q0,q1) end-exclusive
# lease-margin: 1 OK · 0 RED — lease >= k*cadence (the documented cadence*2 convention)
clear-fresh  | age            | fresh=900      | (if (<= age fresh) 1 0)
load-gate    | l1c hour nproc | k=90 q0=1 q1=6 | (if (if (>= hour q0) (< hour q1) 0) 0 (if (> l1c (* k nproc)) 2 1))
lease-margin | cad lease      | k=2            | (if (>= lease (* k cad)) 1 0)
# admitted: 2026-07-23T22:30:13Z via mesh-gate-admission (src disk-free-floor-20260723T223006Z.cand, evaluator b3c917e9)
# consumed: 2026-07-24 by mesh-load-gate's disk-floor axis (the shed gate in front of the heavy
#   reflexes) — the first admitted-then-consumed gate; the admission->consumption loop closes.
disk-free-floor | free_mb | floor=2048 | (if (>= free_mb floor) 1 0)
# --- stage 4a (uxn-hyst-band-ledger 2026-07-23): the band/hysteresis family. -------------
# body-thermal: the phone thermal sense's 4-level hysteresis (COOL 0 · NORMAL 1 · WARM 2 ·
#   HOT 3; p=9 UNKNOWN → snap). t/edges in deci-°C. Consts are CODE-AS-RAN (u1=30 d1=26
#   u2=34 d2=32 u3=38 d3=36 · snap 28/33/37 °C) — the tool's doc header had drifted to a
#   different set; this row is now the one source of truth (mesh-body-thermal resolves it).
# host-therm: hottest kernel zone, deci-°C (was mesh-thermal-zone 45000/70000 milli-C).
# swap/backlight/screen/battery rows: integer-pct bands, verdict = which side (0/1/2[/3]).
#   NOTE the deliberately-VISIBLE same-axis splits: backlight-level 25/70 vs screen-bright
#   30/80 (two panel senses, two calibrations), power-charge 5/20 vs battery-charge 15/25
#   (node-power label vs battery verdict) — unifying either is an operator calibration call,
#   now a one-line diff instead of a two-script hunt.
# diary-stale: mesh-diary's kept-ness budget — same VALUE as clear-fresh's 900 but its OWN
#   row (≈7 missed 2m cadences); sharing the number was coincidence, coupling would make
#   recalibrating one silently move the other.
# vitals-*: mesh-vitals distress flags; vitals-load in centi-load (k=400 ⇒ the old 4*nproc).
body-thermal | t p | u1=300 d1=260 u2=340 d2=320 u3=380 d3=360 s1=280 s2=330 s3=370 | (if (= p 0) (if (> t u1) 1 0) (if (= p 1) (if (< t d1) 0 (if (> t u2) 2 1)) (if (= p 2) (if (< t d2) 1 (if (> t u3) 3 2)) (if (= p 3) (if (< t d3) 2 3) (if (< t s1) 0 (if (<= t s2) 1 (if (<= t s3) 2 3)))))))
host-therm | tdc | lo=450 hi=700 | (if (< tdc lo) 0 (if (< tdc hi) 1 2))
swap-pressure | pct | lo=25 mid=50 hi=80 | (if (< pct lo) 0 (if (< pct mid) 1 (if (< pct hi) 2 3)))
backlight-level | pct | lo=25 hi=70 | (if (< pct lo) 0 (if (< pct hi) 1 2))
screen-bright | pct | lo=30 hi=80 | (if (< pct lo) 0 (if (<= pct hi) 1 2))
power-charge | cap | crit=5 low=20 | (if (< cap crit) 0 (if (< cap low) 1 2))
battery-charge | cap | crit=15 low=25 | (if (< cap crit) 0 (if (< cap low) 1 2))
battery-wear | wear | eol=40 aged=70 | (if (< wear eol) 0 (if (< wear aged) 1 2))
hw-wear-floor | wear | floor=50 | (if (< wear floor) 1 0)
diary-stale | age | budget=900 | (if (> age budget) 1 0)
vitals-disk | pct | max=90 | (if (> pct max) 1 0)
vitals-mem | pct | max=95 | (if (> pct max) 1 0)
vitals-temp | t | max=85 | (if (> t max) 1 0)
vitals-load | l1c nproc | k=400 | (if (> l1c (* k nproc)) 1 0)
# --- uxn-deepening 2026-07-24: the node thermal shed/hold family. ------------------------
# tick-therm: ONE row, TWO consumers by design (mesh-tick THERMAL-SHED skip + mesh-dispatch
#   THERMAL-HOLD defer both read max here — "Threshold reuses tick's band for one knob" was
#   already the doctrine; now the knob is ledger data). t in whole °C. Env order preserved:
#   MESH_DISPATCH_THERMAL_MAX > MESH_TICK_THERMAL_MAX > this row > inline 92.
# tick-offload: the PRE-EMPT band (offload to a cold peer BEFORE the hard shed) — a
#   deliberately-VISIBLE same-axis split vs tick-therm (86 < 92, like backlight/screen-bright):
#   unifying them is an operator calibration call, now a one-line diff.
tick-therm | t | max=92 | (if (>= t max) 1 0)
tick-offload | t | max=86 | (if (>= t max) 1 0)
# vpn-peer-fresh: mesh-vpn-health's WG roster classify (0 active · 1 idle · 2 stale; never=-1
#   stays shell-side, ledger ages are naturals). act=WG-rekey-derived (~2min live ⇒ 300s),
#   idle/stale split at 1h. NOTE 16-bit domain: ages >65535s (≈18h) are NA in the ROM — the
#   shell consumer spans them fine; the ledger is the consts' home, not the runtime evaluator.
vpn-peer-fresh | age | act=300 idle=3600 | (if (< age act) 0 (if (< age idle) 1 2))
# --- uxn-deepening iter-2 2026-07-24: the node memory-pressure band. --------------------
# node-pressure: 1 PRESSURE · 0 OK. ONE row, TWO consumers that until now held the SAME
#   calibration in TWO places coupled only by a COMMENT — mesh-doctor's _sc_mem_exhausted
#   (MESH_DOCTOR_MEMAVAIL_PCT 10 / MESH_DOCTOR_SWAPFREE_PCT 5) said "Mirrors
#   mesh-resource-guard's own NODE-PRESSURE band" while mesh-resource-guard held
#   NODE_MEM_PCT=10 / NODE_SWAP_PCT=5 inline. A comment is not a channel to the reader: the
#   two copies could rot apart and the doctor would defer on a band the guard no longer
#   alerts on. Recalibration is now this one line. Env order preserved per consumer
#   (MESH_DOCTOR_* / MESH_RG_* > this row > inline).
#   Params are already-reduced PERCENTS, not raw kB, because the ROM is 16-bit and MemTotal
#   in kB (≈32e6 here) is far outside the domain — floor(x) < k is exactly x < k for an
#   integer k, so the reduction is lossless at the boundary, not a rounding compromise.
#   hasswap=0 (SwapTotal 0) must never trip the swap leg — a swapless node would read a
#   permanent false PRESSURE (the guard's own documented guard, kept as ledger structure).
node-pressure | apct spct hasswap | mem=10 swap=5 | (if (< apct mem) 1 (if (= hasswap 0) 0 (if (< spct swap) 1 0)))
